---
import BaseLayout from "~/components/layout/BaseLayout.astro";
import { site } from "~/data/site";
const updated = "30 April 2026";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Johannes le Roux Coaching collects, uses, and protects your personal information under POPIA. Lawful basis, retention, and your data rights."
>
  <section class="container-prose py-24">
    <p class="eyebrow eyebrow-red">Legal</p>
    <h1 class="mt-4 display-l">Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-[14px] text-[var(--color-muted)]">Last updated: {updated}.</p>

    <div class="prose mt-12">
      <p>
        This policy explains how <strong>{site.legal.operator}</strong>, trading as
        <em>Johannes le Roux Coaching</em>, collects, uses, stores, and protects personal information
        under South Africa's <strong>Protection of Personal Information Act, 2013 (POPIA)</strong>.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        Responsible party: {site.legal.operator}, {site.address.street}, {site.address.city},
        {site.address.region} {site.address.postalCode}, South Africa.
        Contact: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
        Information Officer: {site.legal.informationOfficer}.
      </p>

      <h2>2. What we collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Enquiry data</strong> — name, email address, the content of your message, and the venture details you choose to share.</li>
        <li><strong>Technical data</strong> — IP address, browser type, pages viewed, and timestamps. Used in aggregate to improve the site.</li>
        <li><strong>Cookies</strong> — essential cookies always; analytics cookies only after you accept the cookie banner.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. Why we collect it</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To respond to your coaching enquiry.</li>
        <li>To provide the coaching services you've engaged us for.</li>
        <li>To comply with legal and tax obligations.</li>
        <li>To improve the site (analytics, only with your consent).</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. Lawful basis</h2>
      <p>
        We process personal information with your consent (s.11(1)(a) POPIA) and where it is
        necessary to perform a contract you've requested (s.11(1)(b)). You can withdraw consent at any time.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Sharing</h2>
      <p>
        We do not sell personal information. We share only with operators that help us run the
        practice — currently a website host (Vercel/Netlify), a form-handling provider (Formspree),
        a scheduling provider (Cal.com), and email infrastructure (Google Workspace) — each of
        which is bound by data-processing terms.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Cross-border transfers</h2>
      <p>
        Some of our processors are based outside South Africa. Personal information is transferred
        only to jurisdictions that provide an adequate level of protection or under equivalent
        contractual safeguards.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Retention</h2>
      <p>
        Enquiry data is retained for 24 months after last contact unless you ask us to delete it
        sooner. Coaching records are retained for the duration of the engagement plus seven years
        for tax and contractual compliance.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Your rights</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Request access to your personal information.</li>
        <li>Correct or delete your personal information.</li>
        <li>Object to processing or withdraw consent.</li>
        <li>Lodge a complaint with the <a href="https://inforegulator.org.za">Information Regulator of South Africa</a>.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>To exercise any of these, email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.</p>

      <h2>9. Security</h2>
      <p>
        Reasonable technical and organisational measures are in place to protect personal information,
        including HTTPS-only transport, access controls, and encrypted storage where supported by our
        operators.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Changes</h2>
      <p>If this policy changes materially, we'll update the date above and notify active clients by email.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
